-- title:
--   Deuring lifting over the Witt disc
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$, and a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $k$ which is elliptic. Let $\beta_0$ be an additive endomorphism of the group $W(k)$ of affine points lying in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), i.e. either $\beta_0 = 0$ or there are bivariate polynomials $n_X, d_X, n_Y, d_Y$ over $k$ and a finite set $B \subseteq k$ such that for every nonsingular point $(x,y)$ with $x \notin B$ the denominators do not vanish and $\beta_0(x,y) = (n_X/d_X,\, n_Y/d_Y)$ evaluated at $(x,y)$. Assume, for $s \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}$, that $\beta_0 \circ \beta_0 + m\cdot\mathrm{id} = s\cdot\beta_0$ on $W(k)$, that $x^2 - sx + m \neq 0$ for every $x \in \mathbb{Z}$, that no prime $\ell$ satisfies both $\ell \mid s$ and $\ell^2 \mid m$, that $m \neq 0$ in $k$, that $m$ is odd and that $m$ is not a square. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$ that is an algebraic extension of $\mathrm{Frac}(W(k))$, the fraction field of the Witt vectors of $k$. Then there exist a valuation subring $B \subseteq \Omega$, a ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $k$ onto the residue field of $B$, a Weierstrass curve $E'$ over $B$ which is elliptic and whose reduction $E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_B$ has nonvanishing discriminant (witness $h_{\Delta'}$), such that the $j$-invariant of $E'$ viewed over $\Omega$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, together with a Weierstrass variable change $v'$ over the residue field with $v' \cdot (E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_B) = W$ transported along $\varphi$ (witness $h_{v'}$), and an element $\beta'$ of [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) for the curve $E'$ over $\Omega$ (same description by rational functions off a finite set) with the following compatibility: for every point $Q$ of $E'$ over $\Omega$ and every $P_0 \in W(k)$, if the image of $P_0$ under the coordinatewise map [`WeierstrassCurve.ratPointHom`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RatPointHom.html#L51) along $\varphi$ equals the image of [`WeierstrassCurve.reduceHom`](def/WeierstrassCurve_ReduceHom.html#L481) $h_{\Delta'}\,Q$ under the inverse of the point bijection [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.equivOfVariableChangeEq`](def/WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv.html#L152) attached to $h_{v'}$, then the same relation holds with $P_0$ replaced by $\beta_0 P_0$ and $Q$ by $\beta' Q$; here `reduceHom` reduces a point whose coordinates lie in $B$ coordinatewise and sends the remaining points to $0$.
--
--   This is the lifting step of Deuring's theorem in the normalised situation (endomorphism satisfying a quadratic relation with norm $m$ odd, non-square, prime to $p$, and with no rational root or non-primitive prime): the pair consisting of the curve and the endomorphism is lifted from characteristic $p$ to a valuation ring of an algebraic extension of the Witt fraction field, the special fibre being identified with $W$ through $\varphi$ and the variable change $v'$, and the lifted curve having $j$-invariant algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul), the step that feeds the lifted data back into the characteristic-zero theory.
